{title: Jingle Bells}
{artist: James Lord Pierpont}
{key: E}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 120}
{tags: Christmas, Fun, Secular, Sing-Along}
{copyright: Public Domain}
{year: 1857}

{comment: Upbeat and fun - great for sing-alongs}

{start_of_chorus}
[E]Jingle bells, jingle bells
Jingle all the way
[A]Oh, what fun it [E]is to ride
In a [B]one-horse open sleigh, hey!
[E]Jingle bells, jingle bells
Jingle all the way
[A]Oh what fun it [E]is to ride
In a [B]one-horse open [E]sleigh
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
[E]Dashing through the snow
In a one-horse open [A]sleigh
O'er the fields we [B]go,
Laughing all the [E]way
[E]Bells on bobtails ring,
Making spirits [A]bright
What fun it is to [B]ride and sing
A sleighing song ton[E]ight, oh!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse}
[E]A day or two ago
I thought I'd take a [A]ride
And soon Miss Fanny [B]Bright
Was seated by my [E]side
[E]The horse was lean and lank
Misfortune seemed his [A]lot
He got into a [B]drifted bank
And then we got up[E]sot
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
